WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.669 --> 00:00:04.910
After months of waiting and speculation, the
full trailer for the eighth and final season

00:00:04.910 --> 00:00:08.900
of Game of Thrones has finally arrived ahead
of the premiere on April 14.

00:00:08.980 --> 00:00:13.460
From dragons at Winterfell to significant
glasses of wine, here are some small details

00:00:13.460 --> 00:00:14.460
you may have missed.

00:00:15.040 --> 00:00:18.860
Greyjoy family infighting took up a lot of
time in the seventh season.

00:00:18.860 --> 00:00:23.080
Good things happened for Theon, who reclaimed
his name after being tortured by Ramsay Bolton.

00:00:23.189 --> 00:00:27.900
But Yara, his formidable older sister, was
captured and held hostage by conniving uncle

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:30.939
Euron, hoping to provoke Theon into retaliating.

00:00:31.120 --> 00:00:35.239
Euron currently holds all the power in the
situation, with his fleet having destroyed

00:00:35.240 --> 00:00:36.120
Yara's ships.

00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:39.989
Though he seems to serve Cersei, it's more
likely that he's simply looking out for his

00:00:39.989 --> 00:00:40.780
own interests.

00:00:41.020 --> 00:00:44.760
It's clear that at least one Greyjoy ship
is on the move in the new trailer, where a

00:00:44.760 --> 00:00:48.560
ship bearing the Greyjoy sigil is seen stocked
with an entire army.

00:00:48.700 --> 00:00:53.039
The leader of the ship is sporting gold armor
and slicked-back blond hair; whoever it is,

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:56.740
it's a sure sign that we haven't seen the
last of the Greyjoy family conflict.

00:00:57.400 --> 00:01:01.659
In the final moments of season seven, the
Night King used his new ice dragon to demolish

00:01:01.660 --> 00:01:05.160
the Wall, setting up an intense scenario for
the final season.

00:01:05.540 --> 00:01:09.420
Viewers were also concerned about the fate
of two characters who were guarding the Wall

00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:12.140
when it fell - Tormund and Beric Dondarrion.

00:01:13.320 --> 00:01:14.300
"It's a long way down."

00:01:14.720 --> 00:01:15.220
"Yeah.

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:17.780
The crows keep telling me I'll get used to
it."

00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:22.799
Fan favorite Tormund has been winning over
audiences for years, so viewers were devastated

00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:24.340
by the possibility of his death.

00:01:24.720 --> 00:01:29.189
But Beric is known for surviving almost anything
through red magic, so it seemed possible that

00:01:29.189 --> 00:01:30.299
he could still be alive.

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:34.920
Thankfully, the trailer gave anxious fans
a glimpse of both Tormund and Beric, flaming

00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:35.920
sword and all.

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:40.520
The most explosive secret revealed during
the sixth season was that Jon Snow is not

00:01:40.520 --> 00:01:45.400
Ned Stark's illegitimate son, but actually
Aegon Targaryen, rightful heir to the Iron

00:01:45.400 --> 00:01:45.900
Throne.

00:01:46.020 --> 00:01:50.540
He's also the nephew to Daenerys Targaryen,
with whom he has recently struck up a new,

00:01:50.540 --> 00:01:51.540
problematic romance.

00:01:51.900 --> 00:01:53.940
"We don't choose whom we love."

00:01:54.420 --> 00:01:58.540
Currently, the lovers remain blissfully ignorant
to their family ties, and the only characters

00:01:58.549 --> 00:02:02.890
with any concrete knowledge of Jon's lineage
are Bran Stark and Sam Tarly, who haven't

00:02:02.890 --> 00:02:04.420
gotten the chance to tell him yet.

00:02:04.580 --> 00:02:08.480
This trailer has a few shots hinting at when
Jon and Daenerys might find out about each

00:02:08.480 --> 00:02:09.480
other.

00:02:09.480 --> 00:02:12.710
There's a moment between the two in the crypts
of Winterfell, where Jon's mother Lyanna is

00:02:12.710 --> 00:02:16.709
buried, as well as a moment with the two of
them approaching the dragons together, which

00:02:16.709 --> 00:02:19.200
might mean Jon is taking a ride on one this
season.

00:02:19.580 --> 00:02:23.820
Jon can also be seen lingering in the godswood,
a place that's been very important to the

00:02:23.820 --> 00:02:24.720
Stark family.

00:02:24.970 --> 00:02:28.920
There's also a shot of Sam and Bran looking
furtively at someone offscreen, which could

00:02:28.920 --> 00:02:32.400
be the moment just before they break the news
to Jon about his new girlfriend.

00:02:33.220 --> 00:02:37.980
The trailer shows both of Daenerys' remaining
dragons arriving at Winterfell, stunning Sansa

00:02:37.980 --> 00:02:39.760
as she stands on the ramparts.

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:43.700
Fans already knew that the dragons would return
for the final season, as they will play an

00:02:43.700 --> 00:02:48.731
instrumental part in the war against the White
Walkers, but Viserion, Daenerys' third dragon

00:02:48.740 --> 00:02:53.120
who fell during a battle with the Night King,
is conspicuously absent from the trailer.

00:02:53.580 --> 00:02:57.620
There's a lot of questions surrounding Viserion's
return, like whether or not Daenerys will

00:02:57.629 --> 00:03:01.069
be able to control him, or if he might return
to his former self.

00:03:01.069 --> 00:03:05.360
In enemy hands, he's a game changer, and leaving
him out of the trailer feels significant.

00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:09.080
Throughout Game of Thrones, Gendry has remained
an enigma.

00:03:09.090 --> 00:03:13.370
As one of the only surviving bastards of King
Robert Baratheon, he has been hunted and in

00:03:13.370 --> 00:03:15.100
hiding for most of the series.

00:03:15.100 --> 00:03:18.950
But though he has a significant claim to the
Iron Throne, he doesn't seem to want control

00:03:18.950 --> 00:03:23.739
of the Seven Kingdoms - as an apprentice blacksmith,
he seems more concerned with surviving than

00:03:23.740 --> 00:03:24.240
ruling.

00:03:24.340 --> 00:03:28.760
Gendry's long absence was resolved in season
seven, with the reveal that he's still working

00:03:28.760 --> 00:03:29.520
as a blacksmith.

00:03:29.840 --> 00:03:33.760
In the season eight trailer, he seems to be
forging swords, which is important in the

00:03:33.769 --> 00:03:35.159
leadup to the final battle.

00:03:35.159 --> 00:03:39.720
With the White Walkers on the move, Westeros
needs Valyrian steel swords more than ever,

00:03:39.720 --> 00:03:42.120
and Gendry may be just the man for the job.

00:03:42.620 --> 00:03:46.900
Audiences see two glimpses of Cersei Lannister
during the trailer, and they couldn't be more

00:03:46.900 --> 00:03:50.980
different - first, she's standing triumphantly
on the shores of King's Landing, flanked by

00:03:50.980 --> 00:03:54.400
the sycophantic Qyburn and her undead bodyguard.

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:56.060
She looks completely in control.

00:03:56.440 --> 00:04:00.870
But in her next shot, she's alone in a quiet
throne room, holding a glass of wine and seemingly

00:04:00.870 --> 00:04:02.020
on the verge of tears.

00:04:02.160 --> 00:04:06.740
Last time we saw Cersei clutching wine on
the Iron Throne, it was during season 2's

00:04:06.750 --> 00:04:10.819
"Blackwater," when she thought the city was
about to fall, so to mimic that moment seems

00:04:10.820 --> 00:04:11.460
significant.

00:04:11.560 --> 00:04:16.239
Also, last season saw her shock her family
by revealing that she was pregnant with Jaime's

00:04:16.240 --> 00:04:16.740
baby.

00:04:16.760 --> 00:04:21.260
After the reveal, she began to conspicuously
decline alcohol, so we have to wonder what

00:04:21.260 --> 00:04:23.520
happens to make Cersei pick up the bottle
again.

00:04:24.240 --> 00:04:28.100
One of the longest-running couples of the
entire show came to an apparent end during

00:04:28.100 --> 00:04:32.830
the seventh season, when Jaime Lannister left
his sister behind to help protect Westeros.

00:04:32.830 --> 00:04:37.120
He's disgusted that Cersei would choose stay
out of the fight against the White Walkers,

00:04:37.120 --> 00:04:42.100
so he leaves King's Landing, apparently heading
to Winterfell to join his brother Tyrion against

00:04:42.100 --> 00:04:43.060
Cersei's wishes.

00:04:43.220 --> 00:04:47.220
Even though there's still time for Jaime to
return to his sister's side, he seems to be

00:04:47.230 --> 00:04:51.580
sticking to his guns in the trailer - though
it's not revealed where he is, fans can guess

00:04:51.580 --> 00:04:55.510
that he may have arrived at Winterfell, as
he tells an unseen character that he promised

00:04:55.510 --> 00:04:57.860
to fight for the living - not just the Lannisters.

00:04:58.100 --> 00:04:59.960
"I intend to keep that promise."

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:04.640
Since Jaime is seen elsewhere in the trailer
bloodied and fighting at a castle that may

00:05:04.640 --> 00:05:08.480
well be Winterfell, it seems like he may just
turn against Cersei after all.

00:05:09.220 --> 00:05:12.880
Throughout the trailer, glimpses of battles
pop up here and there, but thanks to plenty

00:05:12.890 --> 00:05:16.990
of fire and smoke, it's still unconfirmed
where those particular scenes take place.

00:05:16.990 --> 00:05:21.360
However, in the final shot of the trailer,
viewers clearly see Daenerys' Army of Unsullied

00:05:21.360 --> 00:05:26.510
alongside Brienne of Tarth, her loyal squire
Podrick Payne, and Daenerys' closest advisor

00:05:26.510 --> 00:05:31.310
Jorah Mormont waiting in front of Winterfell
as a ghostly horse's leg quietly takes a step

00:05:31.310 --> 00:05:36.330
towards them, indicating the fate of Westeros
may come down to a massive battle at Winterfell,

00:05:36.330 --> 00:05:39.480
where the series introduced us to its world
years ago.

00:05:39.710 --> 00:05:41.780
We hope they've got enough Valyrian steel.

00:05:41.780 --> 00:05:46.320
We know Brienne has a Valyrian sword, but
the rest of the army could be woefully underprepared.

00:05:46.520 --> 00:05:48.160
Hope somebody brought the dragons.

